# fixedbugs, defect 337, lane b11-misc, 2026-10-04.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header whose `#line` names a file holding the byte 0xE9 makes
# clang print every location after it with that byte as it is, and an extern
# the header refutes, `-> i32` over `int64_t`, was `internal error: compiling
# the generated C failed:` over an empty line at exit 2, where the same header
# without the `#line` tells `ffi_return_type` at exit 1.
#
# CAUSE: clang's error stream was read back with `read_file`, which refuses a
# file holding a byte that is not UTF-8, and the refusal was taken for
# silence, so no marker in it was read.
#
# FIX: every reader of clang's words reads them through `cli/read_back.hero`,
# each such byte written by its value, `<0xE9>`.

extern "fixedbugs-337-located.h"
    function wide_count() -> i32  #~ ffi_return_type

function main()
    print(wide_count())
